   ],
   "spoken": "The traditional line: exchange in the centre so Black is left with an isolated queen pawn on d5. That lone pawn is the whole story of the middlegame — a strength in the attack, a weakness in the endgame.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "The Alapin can hand Black an isolated queen pawn — play against it long-term.",
   "plans": "Blockade d5, trade pieces, and target the isolani."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 143.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp3ppp/8/2pp4/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Develop the knight to f3 and follow a simple rule of thumb: wait for Black to commit the dark-squared bishop, and only then capture on c5 — timing the trade so it damages Black's structure most.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Against the IQP, time your captures to fix the weakness, don't rush them.",
   "plans": "Blockade and pile onto d5."
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
